// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Modeling notes (read before validating against the anchor)
//
// DATA, not a runner. `CiPipeline` is the gunbc CI pipeline AS DATA:
// the job/gate dependency DAG (the affected-set-selection surface —
// the load-bearing T-24 concern) as inert structure. The
// `.github/workflows/ci.yml` C4 projection is the eventual goal; v3's
// gate #98 `ci_yml_hand_authority_dissolved` was an open R3 gap and v4
// must not reproduce it.
//
// HONEST SCOPE OF THE C4 CLAIM (INVARIANTS P1 no-fabrication + P2
// single-authority; the affected_set.dag `detect-affected-components.sh`
// interim-bridge precedent). A FAITHFUL `.github/workflows/ci.yml`
// requires GitHub Actions transport facts — `on:` triggers, per-job
// `runs-on:` runners, the `steps:` list (checkout/setup/run),
// concurrency, permissions (workflow-syntax spec) — that `CiPipeline
// { jobs, gates }` deliberately does NOT carry: those are the GHA
// TRANSPORT, not the gunbc job/gate DAG. A `CiPipeline -> ci.yml`
// projection over only jobs/gates would have to FABRICATE every
// trigger/runner/step (INVARIANTS P1/P2).
//
// SINGLE-AUTHORITY SEAM — DEFER to the RATIFIED T-Workflow-As-Data
// path, do NOT mint a parallel one (INVARIANTS P2; the SELF_HOSTING
// authority-audit precedent — review finding 2026-05-16). The ratified
// single authority for the GHA transport is the `Workflow` carrier:
// v3 `extdeps.github.actions { Workflow, Job, RunStep, UsesStep, … }`,
// pinned on `gunbc.ci { CIWorkflowDag }` (regenerated from the
// committed `ci.yml`; "sole live Actions transport for gunbc CI —
// single authority; no hand-parallel `Workflow` mirror"), with
// `WorkflowRuntime = YamlStatic | BinaryShim` deciding arm dispatch and
// the seam `project_github_actions(CIWorkflowDag, WorkflowRuntime) ->
// Workflow` (`dsl/gunbc/ci_emission.dag`). The committed
// `.github/workflows/ci.yml` is that `Workflow` carrier serialized
// under `WorkflowRuntime = YamlStatic` — YAML is DOWNSTREAM of
// `Workflow`, never a parallel `CiPipeline -> YamlValue` projection.
// (An earlier revision of this seam minted `GhaWorkflowSchema` +
// `project_ci_yml -> YamlValue`; that was parallel authority and is
// retracted — provenance, not silently dropped.)
//
// It is NOT fabricated here because no projection is authored: the
// ratified `Workflow` carrier + `WorkflowRuntime`/`project_github_-
// actions` seam are MISSING SUBSTRATE in v4 (v3's
// `extdeps.github.actions` + `dsl/gunbc/ci_emission.dag` have NO v4
// counterpart; minting the v4 counterpart is a NEW extdeps file =
// substrate extension = operator-tier, NOT a worker add — STOP, not
// improvise, and NOT a worker-invented substitute shape). UNTIL that
// substrate exists, the committed `.github/workflows/ci.yml` REMAINS
// the explicit INTERIM HAND-AUTHORED BRIDGE — exactly as
// `scripts/detect-affected-components.sh` is the declared interim
// bridge for affected_set (lens/affected_set.dag header) — and the
// `committed == emit(...)` CHECKED-PROJECTION C4 state is explicitly a
// FUTURE state gated on that named missing ratified substrate, with an
// owner (TRACKED SCAFFOLD (1)), not a property claimed of the present
// `{ jobs, gates }` data.
//
// HEADER TENSION — RECONCILED in-PR (D5). The immutable scaffold
// header (Owns / C4) originally bound BOTH the `CiPipeline { jobs,
// gates }` shape AND a direct "committed == emit(CiPipeline) CHECKED
// PROJECTION" of `.github/workflows/ci.yml`. Those two were in tension:
// the projection cannot be faithful over jobs/gates alone (above).
// Resolving it needs the v4 counterpart of the ratified
// `extdeps.github.actions { Workflow }` carrier + `ci_emission.dag`
// `project_github_actions`/`WorkflowRuntime` seam (new file,
// operator-tier) feeding the projection. Per the DECISIONS.md D5 /
// #3216 standing rule, the operator-tier BLOCKING review actions on
// this PR sanctioned reconciling the frozen header IN-PR: the `Owns`
// "emission target" + C4 lines were reconciled to the single-authority
// `Workflow`-carrier projection with C4 gated on that missing v4
// substrate, and a `HEADER RECONCILE` block (below the Status line)
// cites the actions. C4 operator-ratified intent is preserved; only
// the projection mechanism/source was corrected. This is the honest
// tracked record of that reconcile, not a silent reinterpretation.
//
// WHY job/gate edges are `Symbol`, not inlined sub-nodes. `CiJob.needs`
// and `CiGate.job` are post-resolution opaque `Symbol` references
// (std/node.dag, K-1) to job ids — a job-dependency DAG by NAME, never
// producer-inlining (project_v4_ssa_name_reference_not_inlining: a cyclic
// or shared dependency graph cannot be finitely represented by
// inlining). Affected-set selection (TRACKED SCAFFOLD (2)) traverses
// these `Symbol` edges exactly as lens/affected_set.dag derives its
// graph by `Symbol`-equality traversal.
//
// WHY `command` is a NON-EXECUTABLE faithful `String` (INVARIANTS P1 —
// no fabrication of process facts; codex BLOCKING 2026-05-17). It is
// NOT "the command line the interpreter runs": there is no interpreter
// (the process carrier extdeps/process.dag is T-4.5 SCAFFOLD), and a
// single `String` cannot faithfully carry a GHA job (the live gate is a
// multi-step shell script PLUS a prerequisite `cargo build -p
// v2-compiler --release` step). So `command` is DOCUMENTATION DATA: it
// stores the EXACT primary gate invocation VERBATIM (not a lossy
// paraphrase — the codex finding), and is explicitly NON-EXECUTABLE
// until the process carrier lands. Nothing in this substrate executes
// or branches on it. The faithful FULL step (the `set -euo pipefail` /
// `rm` / `mkdir` / `echo` wrapper + the `cargo build` prerequisite) and
// actual process spawn are the deferred operation carried by
// extdeps/process.dag (T-4.5) + the interpreter (T-22) — TRACKED
// SCAFFOLD (3); they are NOT fabricated into this `String`. Modeled
// like yaml.dag's scalar `lexeme: String` (faithful inert leaf, not a
// sentinel).
//
// TRACKED SCAFFOLD (🟡) — operations deferred with owner + trigger, per
// the operator-ratified declarative-now / operations-deferred discipline
// (std/collection.dag #3169, canonical json.dag #3184). NOT improvised
// bodies, NOT bodiless `fn` (frozen v2 rejects bodiless `fn`, DECISIONS
// PARSE-1):
//   (1) The C4 projection is the RATIFIED single-authority seam
//       `project_github_actions(CIWorkflowDag, WorkflowRuntime) ->
//       Workflow` (NOT a worker-invented `project_ci_yml ->
//       YamlValue`; see SINGLE-AUTHORITY SEAM above — that parallel
//       shape is retracted). `CiPipeline` (this file's gunbc job/gate
//       DAG) FEEDS the ratified `CIWorkflowDag`-pinned `Workflow`
//       carrier; it never invents transport facts (no fabrication,
//       INVARIANTS P1; single authority, P2). The committed
